## Model orchestration

For substantial or risky multi-model work, use `$model-orchestration`. Its `model-routing.md` reference owns the current comparative pool metadata, compatibility constraints, selection axes, and escalation policy; its delegation contract owns writer isolation and orchestration depth.

- Select every call independently from the current model table using task risk, modality and tool compatibility, uncertainty, validation strength, live quota, and observed quality.
- Do not create permanent model-to-role bindings, named model lanes, fixed provider sequences, or automatic task-class defaults. Use the skill's native wrappers and selectors.
- `$local-review` owns review profiles and counts; select each reviewer from the same current table for its concrete failure mode, then use one targeted verification pass after fixes.
- The current session owns scope, synthesis, validation, and acceptance. Workers and reviewers are leaves unless it explicitly authorizes fan-out.
- When running non-interactively through `codex exec` under another orchestrator, implement the assigned task directly and do not re-delegate; the parent owns planning and review.
